From 87d3021c5816813e951ca3eee265946f6072b854 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Vanik <ben.vanik@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:51:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Loom] Separate AMDGPU source capture from memory completion

Scalar address capture does not require VMEM or tensor memory completion
on the supported native targets. Projecting completion onto input
storage retains dead addresses and forces drains before scalar register
reuse.

Generate source leases only for the independent gfx125x X event, keeping
result completion, memory dependencies and vector store-data hazards
separate. This replaces the narrow gfx11 buffer-load exception and
removes the unused write-effect projection without adding runtime
policy.

Cover every native descriptor contract and physical source reuse across
loads, stores, atomics, LDSDMA and tensor transfers. Keep gfx10.1
outside native emission until its distinct scalar-write hazard is
represented.

Backport of upstream c07086aa16fb51ad74c0446a7470d4bc72c60bc8 onto
5927b0e0 with 30246a9d6. This revision has no gfx11 buffer-load capture
exception, so dropping the scalar memory-source leases removes the same
projection from its storage lease builder; gfx125x still keeps its X-event
source leases, and the write-counter mask the projection used goes with
it. This revision has no gfx10.1 native target. Of the new
low_memory_scalar_capture.loom-test cases, those for gfx1170, the gfx125x
X event (whose fixed-register cases this revision's allocator cannot
place, before and after this change) and the global atomic and reduce
mnemonics this revision lacks are left out. Test files that do not exist
here are not added; low_wait_plan and allocation_json take this
revision's output, whose allocation matches upstream's.
